  "_description": "The grandfathering step-up is CAPPED at the sale consideration. Eligible purchase (2017-06-01) with FMV 500 above the sale price of 300. Correct rule: cost = max(100, min(500, 300)) = 300, so gain = (300 - 300) * 10 - 0 = 0 and no loss is created. The previous max(cost_price, fmv) would have taken cost = 500 and manufactured a loss of 2,000 out of a break-even sale. No case in the current dataset trips this (0 of 777 transactions have FMV above sale price), so this guards a latent fault the generator may eventually produce.",
